  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "B. animalis subsp. lactis CNCM I-2494 was routinely cultured in modified-MRS [37], designated here as mMRS, prepared from first principles [peptone from casein, 10 g L−1; meat extract, 10 g L−1 and yeast extract, 5 g L−1 (purchased from Difco); K2HPO4, 3 g L−1; KH2PO4, 3 g L−1; pyruvic acid, 0.2 g L−1; polysorbate 80, 1 ml L−1; tri-ammonium citrate, 2 g L−1; MgSO4.7H2O, 0.575 g L−1; MnSO4.4H2O, 0.12 g L−1; cysteine-HCl, 0.3 g L−1; and FeSO4.7H2O, 0.034 g L−1], and supplemented with 0.05% cysteine-HCl and 1% maltose prior to inoculation."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "B. animalis subsp. lactis CNCM I-2494 (or plasmid-containing derivatives) were cultivated at 4°C under anaerobic conditions which were maintained using an Anaerocult oxygen depleting system (Merck, Darmstadt, Germany) in an anaerobic chamber."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}